%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

POSIX on WebAssembly

or: what is an OS anyway?

%center
%size 3, fore "gray70"
space / click: next    b: back    q: quit
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The dream is old

	2009: Xcerion "icloud" - a desktop in a tab
		file manager, mail, media player, DOS prompt
	the vision ran ahead of the runtime
	16 years later, the runtime caught up
	still at it - daedalOS: 4 years, 4100 commits, solo
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

OS in a browser, 4 ways

%size 4, left, prefix "  ", vgap 60
%fore "yellow"
JS desktop      
%cont, fore "white"
daedalOS - 4 years, solo
%fore "yellow"
x86 emulator    
%cont, fore "white"
v86 - Win95 in a tab
%fore "yellow"
kernel port     
%cont, fore "white"
linux-wasm - 2025
%fore "yellow"
remote stream   
%cont, fore "white"
pixels from a cloud VM
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

gucOS: a fifth way

	an operating system in a browser tab
	no emulator, no JS desktop, no kernel port
	every binary: real C -> a real wasm module
	built by its own compiler, inside it
		emulators pay at every instruction
		gucOS pays only at syscalls
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

This actually runs

%size 6, center, fore "white", vgap 50
DOOM    Quake    SameBoy
lua    sqlite3    busybox
%size 5, fore "yellow"

...and the desktop you are looking at
%size 3, fore "gray70"

the full tour comes at the end
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

What is an OS anyway?

	"it talks to the hardware for you"
	true. one job of many.
	an OS multiplexes the machine:
		CPU - scheduler
		screen - compositor
		audio - mixer
		disk - filesystem
		input - focus
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

What is POSIX?

	the Unix contract. IEEE 1003, 1988.
	files, processes, signals, pipes, terminals
	an API and its semantics
	not a kernel. not a desktop.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

Isn't emscripten POSIX?

	yes: one Unix program, compiled for the browser
	no: one program is not a system
		no processes, no shell, no desktop
	building that is the actual work
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The job list, three ways

%size 4, left, prefix "  ", vgap 45
%fore "SpringGreen"
DO              
%cont, fore "orange"
DON'T           
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
DON'T NEED TO
%fore "SpringGreen"
--------------  
%cont, fore "orange"
--------------  
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
--------------
%pause
%fore "SpringGreen"
processes       
%cont, fore "orange"
threads         
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
a scheduler
%pause
%fore "SpringGreen"
pipes, ptys     
%cont, fore "orange"
fork            
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
drivers
%pause
%fore "SpringGreen"
signals         
%cont, fore "orange"
preemption      
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
an MMU
%pause
%fore "SpringGreen"
a filesystem    
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
                boot
%pause
%fore "SpringGreen"
a desktop       
%cont, fore "DeepSkyBlue"
                ext4
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DO: processes

	one worker per process. own memory.
	pids, pipes, ptys, wait, kill, job control
	spawn, not fork
	pid 1 is busybox hush
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DO: a shared world

	BlockFS - files survive the tab
	a compositor and a window manager
	a sound server - N processes, one output
	cc hello.c inside the OS. it runs.
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T: threads

	no pthreads. no atomics for programs.
	processes are the unit of parallelism
	the kernel underneath is built on both
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T: fork

	fork clones a live process. wasm can't.
	gucOS: posix_spawn
		WSL1 built real fork on NT - its slowest part
		Microsoft's fix was WSL2: a whole VM
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T: preemption

	signals land at safe points
	a busy loop cannot be interrupted
	SIGKILL still works - the worker dies
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T NEED TO: schedule

	gucOS has no scheduler
	each process is a real OS thread
	the machine preempts them. all cores.
	lost: priorities, nice, CPU accounting
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

DON'T NEED TO: the rest

	drivers - the browser has them
	MMU - wasm cannot make a bad address
	boot - the tab is the boot
	ext4 - there is no disk
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%page

The browser is the HAL

%size 3, fore "gray70", center
hardware abstraction layer
%size 5, fore "white", left, prefix 20

display     WebGPU
audio       Web Audio
storage     OPFS
input       browser events
